e-s \"400-840\", :flashinfer-autotune-s \"200-380\", :cuda-graph-capture-s \"~80\"}, :warm-decode-tok-s [37.3 41.9], :cost-per-cold-start-usd \"11-14 (4x B200 @ $25/hr)\", :cost-per-task-once-warm-usd 0.0375, :economic-conclusion \"only viable if batched into one long-lived invocation looping over many tasks; per-task invocation re-pays cold-start tax every time\"}, :cold-start-mitigations-checked {:gpu-memory-snapshots {:reported-speedup \"9-10x elsewhere\", :blocker \"documented incompatible with multi-GPU code; our tensor-parallel-4 setup disqualified, and no GLM-5.2 derivative fits a single GPU\"}, :compile-cache-volume-persistence {:torch-compile-s-before-after [807.65 399.95], :overall-cold-start-s-before-after [1917.8 1570.3], :note \"partial hit only (AOT artifacts reused, inductor/dynamo graph cache key changed between containers); ~50% cut in compile time but only ~18% cut overall since weight-load/autotune/graph-capture are uncached\"}}, :final-decision \"pause route-a here; proceed with route-b (SFT/LoRA-distill Qwen3.6-35B-A3B on GLM-5.2-generated kotoba-lang trajectories), reusing the Stage 0 harness for Stage 1/2\"}", :adr/date "2026-07-07", :adr/amends [], :db/id -1, :adr/problem "{:goal \"kotoba-lang/clj-specialized coding model, ideally deployable on a single 16GB M4 fleet node, preserving GLM-5.2-class agentic coding capability\", :routes-considered {:route-a \"compress GLM-5.2 itself (REAP expert pruning + optional LoRA/SFT recovery + quantize)\", :route-b \"distill into an already-small model (Qwen3.6-35B-A3B) via RAG + GLM-5.2-generated agentic trajectories\"}}", :adr/alternatives "[{:option \"full GLM-5.2 expert pruning + LoRA recovery on Modal B200/H200 multi-GPU\", :verdict :rejected, :reason \"est. $150-600 for training/pruning phase alone, does not reach 16GB target even best-case, no local hardware for LoRA step without ongoing cloud dependency\"} {:option \"deploy Blackwell-cloud-hosted NVFP4 GLM-5.2 derivative instead of local fleet\", 